{
 "duration": 53.426,
 "chunks": [
  {
   "text": "May seventeenth, two thousand six.",
   "start": 0.35,
   "end": 2.577
  },
  {
   "text": "Off the coast of Florida,",
   "start": 2.927,
   "end": 4.484
  },
  {
   "text": "Navy demolition divers set off explosive charges inside a retired American aircraft carrier.",
   "start": 4.604,
   "end": 11.761
  },
  {
   "text": "Thirty-seven minutes later,",
   "start": 12.211,
   "end": 13.747
  },
  {
   "text": "she was gone.",
   "start": 13.867,
   "end": 14.785
  },
  {
   "text": "About nine hundred feet of warship,",
   "start": 15.335,
   "end": 17.436
  },
  {
   "text": "now sitting two hundred and twelve feet down.",
   "start": 17.586,
   "end": 20.076
  },
  {
   "text": "No enemy sank her.",
   "start": 20.576,
   "end": 21.894
  },
  {
   "text": "The United States Navy did.",
   "start": 22.244,
   "end": 24.032
  },
  {
   "text": "On purpose.",
   "start": 24.332,
   "end": 25.256
  },
  {
   "text": "It took three years",
   "start": 26.006,
   "end": 27.197
  },
  {
   "text": "and about twenty million dollars",
   "start": 27.297,
   "end": 29.068
  },
  {
   "text": "just to get her ready to sink.",
   "start": 29.168,
   "end": 30.81
  },
  {
   "text": "So why would the Navy pay millions to send one of its own carriers to the bottom of the sea,",
   "start": 31.36,
   "end": 37.066
  },
  {
   "text": "instead of keeping her,",
   "start": 37.216,
   "end": 38.435
  },
  {
   "text": "or simply cutting her up for scrap?",
   "start": 38.585,
   "end": 40.543
  },
  {
   "text": "The answer starts with what was hidden inside her.",
   "start": 41.143,
   "end": 43.917
  },
  {
   "text": "And this month, a second famous American ship is scheduled to go down off the same coast,",
   "start": 44.517,
   "end": 50.348
  },
  {
   "text": "for the very same reason.",
   "start": 50.498,
   "end": 52.026
  }
 ]
}